  "_note": "Per-language pricing and number format for scripts/make_funnel.py. amount_cents is integer minor units, as everywhere else in this repo. Stripe rules encoded per currency: every amount here is at or above Stripe's minimum charge for that currency, and amount_multiple is the minor-unit step Stripe accepts — HUF is charged in whole forints, so its amounts must be divisible by 100; EUR, CZK, PLN and DKK take any whole minor unit. price_format and decimal_mark are the two optional pricing keys engine.js and reports.py already read. anchor_amount, anchor_format and anchor_group are the value-framing anchor — the one money figure the copy names — in the market's own currency and number convention: anchor_format is written around {n}, anchor_group is the thousands separator (empty for none). The generator writes them to value_framing and swaps the master's literal anchor for the formatted one in every translated string.",
